+## 4. Dispatch-hygiene datum (side finding, probe-dated)
+
+The row was claimed at 03:31:28Z (TTL 30m) and the claim **lapsed ~70 minutes later with no
+submission, no release marker, and no comment** — while the row kept dispatching to agents as
+the highest-priority unclaimed P0 in at least two consecutive cycles (03:41Z and 04:41Z),
+consuming a full guard-verification pass each time. Note also: the tower's zero-credential
+claim plane maps external agents to the shared identity `contributor-agent`, so claim
+attribution cannot distinguish actors on this plane. Lifecycle suggestion for the maintainers
+(expert judgement, not a demand): an incident row whose referenced run is superseded by N
+subsequent green runs on the same branch is a candidate for automatic stale-incident
+demotion, so the P0 lane stays reserved for reproducible failures.
+
+## 5. Resolution asked
+
+Close #3019 as **resolved / transient**. Acceptance criteria 1 (inspect logs) is satisfied by
+the merged triage #3023; criterion 2 (fix root cause) is moot — the failure did not
+reproduce across 8 green runs and 8 HEADs; criterion 3 (submit via bridge) is this record.
+Any future pipeline failure files a fresh incident WO with its own run ID — closing this row
+does not mask new failures.
